D) The bar remainder went from _mix(SURFACE,ACCENT,0.75) (#4580C4) to 0.35 (#264365): the consumed/remaining step goes 1.62:1 -> 4.01:1. With a dark track one ink no longer serves both halves, so each label is now drawn twice on a bar-sized layer and split pixel-exactly at the fill edge - SURFACE (7.69:1) over the bright fill, INK (8.40:1) over the dark track. A label straddling the edge is the normal case, not a corner one.

Also fixed a collision that change C made reachable: at four bars "Session 100%" + "10h05m" printed over each other. The countdown now gives way when the pair does not fit, and an over-long scoped name truncates while keeping its percentage.

